# Phase 5 Wave E: upper-secondary basic science (ม.4-ม.6), opened 2026-09-18.
# Slice 1 opens ว 2.1 ม.5 with the atomic-structure cluster: ม.5/1 (ธาตุ/สารประกอบ
# and อะตอม/โมเลกุล/ไอออน from a chemical formula), ม.5/2 (the Bohr model vs the
# electron-cloud model), and ม.5/4 (writing a nuclide symbol and identifying an
# isotope — two free verbs, so both Foundation and Fluency are exact). Slice 2
# adds ม.5/5 (หมู่/คาบ and metal/nonmetal/metalloid/representative/transition
# classification), ม.5/6 (conductivity and electron-giving/receiving between
# metals and nonmetals), and ม.5/7 (benefit/hazard examples for representative
# and transition elements). Slice 3 adds ม.5/8 (bond order and shared-pair
# count), ม.5/9 (polarity of two-atom molecules), and ม.5/10 (hydrogen-bond
# capability from a structural formula). Slice 4 adds ม.5/11 (boiling point
# vs intermolecular force), ม.5/12 (writing ion and ionic-compound formulas),
# and ม.5/13 (dissociation and electrolyte/nonelectrolyte classification).
# Slice 5 adds ม.5/14 (saturated/unsaturated hydrocarbons), ม.5/15 (polymer
# vs monomer physical properties), and ม.5/16 (acid-base from organic
# structure). Slice 6 adds ม.5/17 (solubility in various solvents), ม.5/18
# (thermoplastic vs thermoset structure and use), and ม.5/19 (polymer-product
# impact on life and the environment, with mitigation). Slice 7 adds
# ว 2.2 ม.5/2 (vectors). Slice 8 adds ม.5/20 (chemical equations), ม.5/21 and
# ม.5/22 (rate of reaction); slice 9 closes ว 2.1 ม.5 with ม.5/23 (redox),
# ม.5/24 (radioactivity and half-life) and ม.5/25 (radioisotope uses and
# protection); slice 10 adds ว 2.2 ม.5/1 (acceleration from velocity-time data).
